{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Collaboration95/rewind-app/pulls/595","id":5019492233,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUL2vfc8AAAABKy9fiQ","html_url":"https://github.com/Collaboration95/rewind-app/pull/595","diff_url":"https://github.com/Collaboration95/rewind-app/pull/595.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/Collaboration95/rewind-app/pull/595.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Collaboration95/rewind-app/issues/595","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Collaboration95/rewind-app/pulls/595/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Collaboration95/rewind-app/pulls/595/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Collaboration95/rewind-app/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Collaboration95/rewind-app/issues/595/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/Collaboration95/rewind-app/statuses/38593b225cf636062f2b1578ccfcc033f86fbd64","number":595,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"ci: retain DevSecOps artifacts for verified dev releases","user":{"login":"Collaboration95","id":68595032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4NTk1MDMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68595032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Collaboration95","html_url":"https://github.com/Collaboration95","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Collaboration95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Collaboration95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Collaboration95/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Collaboration95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Collaboration95/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Collaboration95/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Collaboration95/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Collaboration95/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Collaboration95/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Dev deployments previously rebuilt images without scanning the bundle that would actually be installed, and Quality did not retain test/audit reports. This batch adds visible security stages and evidence tied to the exact commit and release bytes for the course pipeline demonstration.\n\n- **A2 — DAST:** retain the post-deploy, unauthenticated, report-only ZAP baseline; show JSON/HTML/Markdown availability and findings in its job summary. Artifact: `zap-baseline-<commit>` (`report_json.json`, `report_html.html`, `report_md.md`).\n- **A3 — scan what ships:** Trivy **v0.70.0**, matching Release security, scans `runtime.tar` and `web.tar` extracted by the existing bundle verifier. Require matching image IDs, Alpine OS results and a nonempty package inventory (`--list-all-pkgs`); retain both images' results and fail HIGH/CRITICAL before any host upload. Artifact: `dev-release-security-<commit>` (`sbom-runtime.cdx.json`, `sbom-web.cdx.json`, `trivy-runtime.json`, `trivy-web.json`).\n- **A4 — provenance:** SHA-pinned `actions/attest-build-provenance` attests both the tarball and security manifest. Grant `id-token: write` and `attestations: write` only to the deploy job. Artifact: `dev-release-bundle-<commit>` (tarball plus Sigstore JSON attestation bundle), also linked from the job summary.\n- **A5 — manifest:** `release-manifest.json` in `dev-release-security-<commit>` records commit, workflow/run/attempt, successful Quality run ID, timestamp, image IDs/archive digests/available OCI and repository digests, vulnerability counts, and SHA-256 of bundle, both SBOMs and both JSON reports. Retain it in Actions; host installer unchanged.\n- **A6 — Quality evidence:** root/server JUnit XML, server coverage JSON plus existing V8/text coverage, frontend native Jest results JSON and coverage summary, and production audit JSON, with per-job summary tables. Artifacts: `quality-test-results-root`, `server-coverage`, `frontend-coverage`, `quality-npm-audit`. `jest-junit` is absent, so no frontend JUnit dependency is added. Keep the required `Format, lint, typecheck, and test` name, its `needs`, docs-only skips, audit severity and coverage gates unchanged.\n- **A7 — secrets:** standalone PR/dev/main full-history Docker Gitleaks v8.30.1 scan, default rules extended with two path-AND-exact-value allowlists for five historical non-credential values. Artifact: `gitleaks-<commit>` (`gitleaks.sarif`, redacted), also uploaded to code scanning with the repository's pinned CodeQL action. Fork PRs retain the artifact without requesting a write-token upload.\n- **A8 — security triggers:** Release security now runs on dev/main pushes as well as existing filtered PRs, version tags and manual dispatch. Existing artifacts: `release-security-runtime-<commit>`, `release-security-web-<commit>`, `release-security-iac-<commit>`.\n- Add **Pipeline artifacts** and update affected pipeline descriptions in `docs/site/content/cicd.json`; no other site pages changed.\n\nValidation: changed YAML passes Prettier and actionlint; root and fast suites pass; Python security boundary tests cover severity blocking, wrong scan identity, incomplete OS/package scans and scanner failure; local full-history Gitleaks exits 0; lint/architecture/typecheck pass (two existing native-build import warnings). Saved-image JSON and CycloneDX generation were exercised using Docker Trivy v0.70.0 on an existing local image; its reported ImageID matches that saved image. This compatibility check is separate from current-release proof.\n\nMerged `origin/dev` after #591 to include the dependency/image fixes and FFmpeg setup changes. The coordinator owns merging this PR. Exact-bundle deploy scans, GitHub attestations and hosted ZAP need the post-merge Deploy dev run; PR/local checks do not establish deployed success. Only aggregate Quality is required by existing branch protection; ZAP findings remain report-only.\n\nOne GPT-6.1 Sol review pass found incomplete-scan acceptance and overbroad secret exceptions. Both are fixed with negative fixtures: missing OS metadata, language-only scans and empty inventories fail closed; new synthetic credentials in the previously exempted schema/db/test paths still fail Gitleaks.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-26T14:50:40Z","updated_at":"2026-10-26T14:55:29Z","closed_at":"2026-10-26T14:55:29Z","merged_at":"2026-10-26T14:55:29Z","merge_commit_sha":"aea7478bce14131b821caaa99b1185077b4a9403","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"Collaboration95:guru/devsecops-artifacts","ref":"guru/devsecops-artifacts","repo":{"id":1354608509,"node_id":"R_kgDOUL2vfQ","name":"rewind-app","full_name":"Collaboration95/rewind-app","owner":{"login":"Collaboration95","id":68595032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY4NTk1MDMy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/68595032?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Collaboration95","html_url":"https://github.com/Collaboration95","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Collaboration95/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Collaboration95/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Collaboration95/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Collaboration95/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Collaboration95/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Collaboration95/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Collaboration95/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Collaboration95/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Collaboration95/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"Rewind helps close-knit groups capture everyday moments an